## 2. Colour

OKLCH, [light/dark]-first. Shared surface ladder and status vocabulary apply
unchanged (see shared-design-language.md §2 and §3). The only brand choice here
is the primary accent.

### Primary accent

The primary is the ONE brand accent. It appears on:
- The primary action in any context (one per `PageHeader`)
- The active nav item
- Focus rings (`--ds-color-ring` aliases `--ds-color-primary`)
- OPTIONALLY: [list any other deliberate use; keep it short]

Nowhere decorative. No second accent.

### Status palette (binding — do not redefine)

| Token | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `--ds-color-status-success` | done, healthy, confirmed |
| `--ds-color-status-warning` | needs attention, awaiting input, expiring |
| `--ds-color-status-error` | failed, expired, revoked, destructive |
| `--ds-color-status-info` | in-flight, processing, informational |
| `--ds-color-status-neutral` | idle, queued, skipped, inactive |

Applied as: a coloured dot or icon **plus a label** (WCAG 1.4.1 — never colour
alone). Badge text at full chroma on a `~14%` same-hue tint. Never flood-fill a
row. The single component for this is `StatusBadge`.

---

## 3. Typography

Three faces, each with one job. Families are binding; do not substitute.

| Role | Family | Used for |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Display** | Fraunces | Page titles, wordmarks, empty-state headings, large readouts |
| **Body / UI** | Hanken Grotesk | Everything textual: labels, descriptions, table cells, buttons, nav |
| **Data / Mono** | JetBrains Mono | Machine-produced values only: IDs, hashes, ISO dates, amounts, counts |

Scale (fill in the values the app actually uses; delete roles that do not apply):

| Name | Size | Weight | Line-height | Use |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `display-l` | 1.75rem | 600 | 2.125rem | Page title |
| `heading` | 1.125rem | 600 | 1.625rem | Card / section title |
| `body` | 0.9375rem | 400 | 1.4 | Default UI text |
| `small` | 0.8125rem | 400 | 1.25 | Secondary text, table cells |
| `label` | 0.6875rem | 600 | 1 | Uppercase eyebrow, column heads |
| `mono-data` | 0.875rem | 400 | 1.25 | IDs, timestamps, values (tabular) |

Rules: any value a machine produced = `font-code` + tabular figures (`tnum`).
Body copy caps at ~70ch. Never mono for prose.

