## 6. Components

Built on shadcn-svelte primitives (mandatory). Shared primitives from
`src/lib/components/` — see shared-design-language.md §4 for the full contract.
Document APP_NAME-specific additions or deviations below.

REPLACE or extend this list with the components actually used:

- **`Button`** — shadcn `ui/button` only. One primary (`default`) per `PageHeader`. Never hand-roll.
- **`StatusBadge`** — dot + label on a ~14% same-hue tint. The only state chip.
- **`PageHeader`** — `{ title, subtitle?, eyebrow?, breadcrumbs?, actions? }`. One primary action.
- **`DataTable`** — shadcn table primitives; `label` column heads; mono data cells.
- **`StatList`** — route metrics as a vertical label→value list. Zero-aware.
- **`DetailPanel`** — entity detail (header + scrollable body + sticky footer).
- **`EmptyState`** — Fraunces heading, muted line, primary CTA.

Icons: `@lucide/svelte`, deep imports, `size-4` inline / `size-5` standalone /
`size-6` empty states. Every status glyph pairs with a label and a colour.

---

## 7. Do / Don't

**Do:**
- Compose from shared primitives; add to the shared library when a new one is needed
- Use `StatusBadge` for every state chip (dot + label, never colour alone)
- Use `--ds-color-primary` for the one action accent and the active nav item
- Use mono + tabular figures for any machine-produced value
- Let tables run full width; cap forms at `max-w-2xl`
- Apply `--ds-radius-lg` to cards; `--ds-radius-xl` to dialogues
- Use `--ds-font-display` (Fraunces) for page titles and empty-state headings

**Don't:**
- Centre a narrow column on a wide screen
- Add a second accent colour
- Flood-fill table rows with a status colour
- Use colour as the only state signal (WCAG 1.4.1)
- Use mono for prose or body copy
- Hand-roll a `<button>` where a shadcn `Button` variant applies
- Put two primary actions in one `PageHeader`
- Write raw oklch / hex values in a component — every colour is a `--ds-*` var

